## 7. MCP, scene store and captures

Extend existing draw/update/read tools for terrain nodes and modifier settings, with validation, batch refs, compact results and dry runs. Resolve `source` references on creation/copy like other node dependencies. Reordering must be available to the agent through the existing store's placement operation; expose that operation through MCP if it is not already available, rather than inventing a second ordering system.

`get_scene` and `find_nodes` show terrain identity, source group, bounds, resolution, cell spacing and generated elevation range. Source modifier settings remain readable in their outliner order. Never return the full sample array in ordinary tool responses. Add `get_guide terrains`, documenting order, visibility/export behavior, supported geometry and deferred surface queries.

The store remains the source of truth. One draw/update/reorder/copy action is one undo step; regeneration does not add a second history entry. Persistence, reload, hidden nodes and failed/dry-run edits need coverage.

Captures and `render_view` display the generated mesh without source overlays by the end of the phase. Until terrain-aware query integration lands, tools that cannot account for terrain must explicitly report that limitation when it affects their result; do not present checks against source shapes as verified terrain checks. Avoid changing query algorithms as part of this authoring phase.

