## 9. Increments

### 16.1 — Tiny terrain editor, smoothing experiment and first Unity export

- Terrain/source schemas and minimal persistence/history; boxes and cylinders as contributors; Raise/Lower/Set and Fade; outliner evaluation order.
- Minimal creation and inspector controls, generated mesh, editable visible sources and Show modifiers. Use the existing reorder UI.
- Perform §4's experiments, record the chosen behavior, and export/import a native Unity Terrain. Move a shape and manually sync again.
- **Checks:** flat baseline, plateau interior, fade boundary/zero, overlap/reorder, negative heights, deterministic browser/server samples, Unity row direction/range and source omission; undo/reload of the small fixture.
- **Browser/Unity:** create a hill, soften its edge, move it, inspect ground alone, export, and see the same ground as a native Terrain with a working collider. Repeat after an edit. No Walk integration, worker framework or full query integration in this increment.

### 16.2 — Free-forms, smooth ramps and complete editing

- Free-form and smooth-ramp projection; finish the rectangle drawing tool, Make terrain and influence outlines.
- Complete nested hierarchy order, copy/clipboard reference remapping, group changes, transforms and deletion rules.
- **Checks:** concave outline, curved path, reordered nested groups, collapse independence, hide versus Show modifiers, transform refusal without partial edits, clone independence and undo.
- **Browser:** two hills, a courtyard and winding rising path; moving their existing handles reshapes the terrain. Reorder the courtyard above/below the hills and undo.

### 16.3 — Agent workflow, captures and measured responsiveness

- Complete MCP/read results, ordering access, dry runs and guide; clean captures/shot rendering.
- Benchmark and implement only the caching/worker/preview work required for usable editing. Canonical results and revision handling are mandatory if previews become asynchronous.
- **Checks:** batch refs, invalid ownership, failed/dry-run calls, rendered/exported parity, stale jobs if applicable, 20/100-modifier measurements.
- **Browser/agent:** the agent makes and reorders a small terrain, the human edits it, and both inspect the generated result through captures.

### 16.4 — Unity refresh, GLB and acceptance

- Stable assets, content drift, full claims/deletion/undo/Auto sync handling, GLB mesh and export compatibility tests.
- **Checks:** manual and automatic refresh, unmodified terrain untouched, claimed terrain preserved, local sculpt detected, removed source objects with Unity additions preserved appropriately, negative/nonzero coordinate fixture, GLB parity.
- **Browser/Unity:** the full §1 loop and §11 checklist. Record any remaining limitations; terrain-aware walking is tracked separately, not a reason to leave this phase unfinished.

